From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shivani Agarwal <shivani.agarwal@broadcom.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] intel/jay: Fix build with GCC 12 lacking C23 fixed
 underlying type enums

jay_ir.h declares "enum jay_predication : uint8_t", a C23 feature
(fixed underlying type for enums). GCC only supports this in C mode
starting with GCC 13; Photon's toolchain is GCC 12.2.0, so jay_ir.h
fails to compile:

  jay_ir.h:521:22: error: expected identifier or '(' before ':' token
  jay_ir.h:595:25: error: field 'predication' has incomplete type
  jay_ir.h:645:29: error: 'JAY_PREDICATED_DEFAULT' undeclared

struct jay_inst embeds this enum as a plain field and is guarded by

  static_assert(sizeof(jay_inst) == 32 + (sizeof(uintptr_t) * 2), "packed");

so the enum's storage size must stay at 1 byte. Simply dropping the
":uint8_t" annotation lets the enum fall back to int-sized storage
and breaks that static_assert. Use GCC/Clang's
__attribute__((packed)) on the enum instead, which forces the
smallest integer type that fits the enumerators (1 byte here, since
all values are 0-2) without requiring C23 syntax.
---
 src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_ir.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_ir.h b/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_ir.h
--- a/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_ir.h
+++ b/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_ir.h
@@ -518,7 +518,7 @@
    return jay_base_type(t) == JAY_TYPE_F || jay_base_type(t) == JAY_TYPE_BF;
 }

-enum jay_predication : uint8_t {
+enum jay_predication {
    /** No predication. */
    JAY_NOT_PREDICATED = 0,

@@ -530,7 +530,7 @@

    /** Predicated with 1 default value. Used pre-RA. */
    JAY_PREDICATED_DEFAULT = 2,
-};
+} __attribute__((packed));

 /**
  * Representation of a shader instruction in the Jay IR.
--
2.43.0
